#NUBITS 16
#NUIOIN 1
#NUIOOU 32
// A port number wider than the data address and the operand (2026-10-19).
// Two variables and two constants: the data address has 2 bits, and with
// about 14 instructions the operand had 4. Port 31 needs 5. The port number
// came to io_ctrl cut to the data-address width (core.v), and asmcomp sized
// the operand from the memories only: before the fix nothing came out on
// ports 31 and 9 (out_en was x). Each input word must come out on port 31,
// the next on port 9, three times each.
void main()
{
    int k;
    for (k = 0; k < 3; k = k + 1)
    {
        out(31, in(0));
        out(9, in(0));
    }
}
